              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#overviews"} Overviews
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#homotopy_theory_of_dgcategories"} Homotopy theory of dg-categories
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#derived_noncommutative_geometry"} Derived noncommutative geometry
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#other_aspects"} Other aspects
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Differential graded categories
            or
            %em dg-categories
            are linear analogues of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+categories"} spectral categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} linear
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+categories"} enhanced triangulated categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em dg-category
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} enriched
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (infinity,1)-category of chain complexes
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} strictly enriched
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Haugseng13"} Haugseng 13
          %p
            Hence a dg-category is a category with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+complexes"} mapping complexes
            of morphisms between any two objects. By taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homologies"} homologies
            of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            in degree zero, one gets an ordinary category, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+dg-category"} homotopy category of a dg-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#the_infinity1category_of_dgcategories The (infinity,1)-category of dg-categories
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+model+structure+on+dg-categories"} Dwyer-Kan model structure on dg-categories
            presents the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+dg-categories"} (infinity,1)-category of dg-categories
          %h3#relation_to_stable_categories
            Relation to stable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of dg-categories is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} enriched
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} modules
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Mac+Lane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-Mac Lane spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} linear
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
          %p
            More precisely, it is shown in
            %a{:href => "#Cohn13"} Cohn 13
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+model+structure+on+dg-categories"} Morita model structure on dg-categories
            presents the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+complete+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} idempotent complete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} linear
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
          %h2#aspects_of_dgcategories Aspects of dg-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+dg-category"}> homotopy category of a dg-category
              \.
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+dg-categories"} equivalence of dg-categories
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"}> dg-modules
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+dg-modules"} perfect dg-modules
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+dg-category"} derived dg-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Yoneda+embedding"} dg-Yoneda embedding
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretriangulated+dg-category"} pretriangulated dg-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-localization"}> dg-localization
              ,
              %span.newWikiWord
                dg-quotient
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/dg-quotient"} ?
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-nerve"} dg-nerve
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+K-theory+of+a+dg-category"} Waldhausen K-theory of a dg-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-topological+K-theory+of+a+dg-category"} semi-topological K-theory of a dg-category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+moduli+stack+of+objects+in+a+dg-category"} derived moduli stack of objects in a dg-category
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} enhanced triangulated category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+category"} A-infinity category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+category"} spectral category
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
          %h2#references References
          %p Historically, dg-categories were introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+M.+Kelly"}> G. M. Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chain maps inducing zero homology maps
              %strong 61
              (1965), 847–854, doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100039207"} 10.1017/S0305004100039207
          %p whilst their modern development can be traced to
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                A. I. Bondal
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/A.+I.+Bondal"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"} Mikhail Kapranov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Enhanced triangulated categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/bondalKaprEnhTRiangCat.pdf", :title => "Bondal-Kapranov Enhanced triangulated categories pdf"} Bondal-Kapranov Enhanced triangulated categories pdf
          %p A bicategory refinement
          %ul
            %li
              Yuki Imamura.
              %em A formal categorical approach to the homotopy theory of dg categories
              (2024). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.07873"}> arXiv:2405.07873
              ).
          %h3#overviews Overviews
          %p For concise reviews of the theory, see section 1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Beilinson"}> A. Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V.+Vologodsky"} V. Vologodsky
              = succeed "." do
                %em DG guide to Voevodsky’s motives
          %p as well as the introduction and appendices to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V.+Drinfeld"}> V. Drinfeld
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em DG quotients of DG categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~gaitsgde/grad_2009/DGquotients.pdf"} pdf
          %p For longer surveys, see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Keller"}> Bernhard Keller
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On differential graded categories
              %strong II
              (2006) 151-190, Eur. Math. Soc., Zürich &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601185"}> arXiv:math/0601185
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              %em Lectures on dg-categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://perso.math.univ-toulouse.fr/btoen/files/2012/04/swisk.pdf"}> pdf
              ).
          %h3#homotopy_theory_of_dgcategories Homotopy theory of dg-categories
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
            is studied in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gon%C3%A7alo+Tabuada"}> Gonçalo Tabuada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Théorie homotopique des DG-caté́gories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0710.4303.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gon%C3%A7alo+Tabuada"}> Gonçalo Tabuada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Une structure de catégorie de modèles de Quillen sur la catégorie des dg-catégories
          %p
            The equivalence with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Cohn13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lee+Cohn"}> Lee Cohn
              ,
              %em Differential Graded Categories are k-linear Stable Infinity Categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.2587"}> arXiv:1308.2587
              )
          %p
            (Note that the proof works over any ring, even though it is stated there for
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          %p
            In the following it is shown that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
            enriched in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of ordinary categories strictly enriched in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %ul
            %li#Haugseng13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rectification of enriched infinity-categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.3881v2"} arXiv:1312.3881
          %h3#derived_noncommutative_geometry Derived noncommutative geometry
          %p
            The following references discuss the use of dg-categories in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} derived noncommutative algebraic geometry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+motives"} noncommutative motives
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gon%C3%A7alo+Tabuada"}> Gonçalo Tabuada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Invariants additifs de DG-catégories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Robalo"}> Marco Robalo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Théorie homotopique motivique des espaces noncommutatifs
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~marco.robalo/these.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                S. Mahanta,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative geometry in the framework of differential graded categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.1628"} arXiv:0805.1628
            %li
              %p
                D. Orlov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Smooth and proper noncommutative schemes and gluing of DG categories
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2016.07.014"} doi
          %h3#other_aspects Other aspects
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Keller"}> Bernhard Keller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deriving DG categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=ASENS_1994_4_27_1_63_0"} numdam
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Tamarkin"}> Dmitry Tamarkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What do dg-categories form?
              %p Compos. Math. 143 (2007), no. 5, 1335–1358.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Batanin"}> M. Batanin
                ,
                %em What do dg-categories form
                (after Tamarkin), talks at Paris 7 and Australian category seminar (
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.usyd.edu.au/u/AusCat/abstracts/060726mb.html"}> abstract
                ),
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0606553"} math.CT/0606553
            %li
              %p
